      "id": "2073914501213389167",
      "text": "I had one task involving a @threejs  effect that Fable one-shotted. Apart from that, I’ve found Opus, especially in UltraCode mode, to be really strong. I’d say it’s maybe comparable to Fable. Fable seems to excel when the task is very ambiguous and you need to build a large system from scratch. It does really well in maintaining huge contexts and still figuring delivering amazing results . Opus degrades in performance when context starts growing.",
